A||N||22||jhogans||V8 Engines||||10
Z||000000||jhogans||09-15-1999||09:56 AM||||Hey Fiero Lovers.  I'm new to this forum.  I just found it while surfing the web gathering information on the Fiero.<P>The wife gave me the go to buy a new Honda Civic CX Hatchback.  I am planning to compete at car shows and audio shows with the new car.  I am going to add aftermarket stuff to the car such as filters, rims, stereo system, etc.<P>By chance I happen to come across a couple web pages about Fieros.  It brought back these child hood dreams of owning one.  I read that people are putting V8s in the Fieros.  I was amazed and drooling at the same time.  I have always wanted a sports car and I thought if I got a Fiero with a V8 I would be on my way  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I looked at V8 Archies Website, <A HREF="http://www.v8archie.com," TARGET=_blank>http://www.v8archie.com,</A>  Design 1 Website (Northstar Engine conversion), <A HREF="http://www.design1systems.com," TARGET=_blank>http://www.design1systems.com,</A>  and American Custom Engineering (Northstar), <A HREF="http://www.americancustomeng.com." TARGET=_blank>http://www.americancustomeng.com.</A>   Engine swapping on the Civic is so common that it is natural.<P>I have a couple of questions:<P>1 - Are there any problems doing this?<P>2 - Has anybody on this forum have a V8 Fiero or knows anybody that does?<P>3 - If yes to Q3, How do you like?  Is it worth it?<P>4 - Are small block Chevys and Northstar engines the only V8s you can use?<P>5 - Do I need to change the transmission if a V8 is used?<P>6 - Does it matter if I use an automatic or manual?<P>7 - Do I need to change the exhaust system?<P>8 - What should I look for when purchasing a used Fiero? ie, newest model<P>9 - What other concerns should I have pertaining to this issue?<P>10 - What should I expect to pay for a used Fiero?<P>The last problem is trying to convince the wife in letting me buy a Fiero.  She said that the car was too small for me.  I have a football player build, 5'10" - 270lbs.  I told her that the Civic can't be any bigger.  I left the same message on alt.autos.fiero.  There are guys that are about the same size and they have no problems.  Therefore, I just need to try to convince the wife again.<P>Thanks for any info guys.||||reg||10
Z||000001||FieroSTETZ||09-15-1999||10:53 AM||||All that I can tell you is this... You can't be too big for a fiero. I am 6'4" 220 lbs, and i fit fine in my '86 SE.||||reg||1
Z||000002||BENGAL4||09-15-1999||01:01 PM||||Tell her that I am 6' 1", 270 lbs. It is very comfortable to ride in. You ought to see me and my buddy Fred ride in the car. He is 6' 4", 330 lbs. From behind, I bet other drivers thinks it's one body with two heads. Fiero over Honda, that's the only choice no matter what size you are. ||||reg||10
Z||000003||RICK||09-15-1999||01:21 PM||||I got you all on this one...5'10" 350+ and no problems except for when I hit a big bump and then I hit my head on the sunroof...ouch||||reg||14
Z||000004||lowCG||09-15-1999||01:34 PM||||Well I'm not real big,but I bought a car without the sunroof,hoping for more helmet clearance.||||reg||1
Z||000005||batboy||09-15-1999||02:51 PM||||If I were you, I'd find a Fiero for sale and take it out for a test drive with the wife and see for yourselves about the comfort and fit. Prices vary depending on the condition and geographical region. Go to the mall in this Forum, there are several good cars for sale there. If you want an extremely nice, fast Fiero needing no work, Greendano has a really great one for sale. Pictures of his yellow car are all over the web.<P>About V8 Fieros: Yes, there are problems. Yes, I have one. The Chevy small block and the Caddy Northstar are the only two V8s that have kits that I know about. You have to use the Fiero tranny. You can use either the manual or auto tranny. Yes, the exhaust must be changed. I think everyone agrees the 1988 model is the best and the 1984 model is the least desireable (except the Indy car). The V8 conversion is very expensive and does affect handling. Email me if you want details.||||reg||1
Z||000006||jhogans||09-17-1999||05:44 PM||||Fiero Lovers,<P>I tried to convince my wife but it was a no go.  I am feeling down now.  I really wanted me a Fiero.  She used every excuse out there.  I printed out the replys I had from my size that own Fiero's but that didn't seem to phase her.  She said where are the kids going to sit.  I was like WHAT!! That is why I just bought you a new Accord (I thought to myself).  I didn't tell her this because I knew I would get drilled.  I just gave up because I new it was a dead end.<P>I appreciate everybody replying to my message.  I have learned lots of things about the Fiero from reading this forum and all of the Websites out there.  I will keep reading this forum in hopes that my wife will change her mind.<P>Thanks for all of the info.||||reg||9
Z||000007||batboy||09-17-1999||10:05 PM||||Bummer! Time to get a new wife that likes Fieros, haha.||||reg||1
Z||000008||88 Fiero||09-17-1999||10:27 PM||||Jhogans...I think you should tell your wife and let her know that you work too...and that you deserve something out of your sweat and blood...that's what I told mine and now she doesn't want me to get rid of my ride...It's just fair that we men had to have something to tinker around and for me it rather be a fiero than another woman....||||reg||6
Z||000009||Patrick||09-18-1999||01:23 AM||||<BR>Mr. Hogans, you weigh 270 lbs and your wife is telling you what kind of car you may or may not have??!!!<P>Don't get me wrong, I'm NOT suggesting that you should pound her into submission, but I doubt it's the case that she could do that to you if you bought the car you wanted.<P>What difference would it really make to your wife whatever car you bought? She has her own vehicle. You have your own job. I can't believe that people allow themselves to be ordered around like this. <P>I guess that's why I've always been single. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>||||reg||9
Z||000010||batboy||09-18-1999||08:46 AM||||Come on guys, don't be so rough on him. Marriage is a two way street. Not only is having mutual consent when it comes to major purchases the right thing to do in a relationship, but he'll be sleeping on the sofa for the next year if he doesn't have complete agreement. I still don't know what the harm is in JUST taking a test drive. No obligation, only a quick cruise. Maybe she'll fall in love with it too. The worst that can happen is that she will still say no. Plus you get to drive a Fiero to see what they're really about. Good luck dude.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Phil||09-18-1999||10:16 AM||||Fortunately my wife thinks the Fieros are "cute" and we just drove from Rhode Island to Key West Florida and back in my 88 Formula and she had no complaints at all. Take a test drive. BTW I'm 6'1" 210lbs.and my car is dropped 1". ||||reg||1
Z||000012||terryk||09-18-1999||10:09 PM||||Here's my story. I'm 45, married 23 years. I do try to make it mutual or make sure I'm not ignoring my wife's view of everything.<P>I said for about 1 year, that I would buy a Fiero if a nice one came along. The wife couldn't understand why I wanted one and thought it was silly, but hey if it keeps me out of trouble.... I bought a nice 86 V6 SE.<P>I've driven it 1/10 what she drives it. I basically have to look for another one now. I'll never get this one back from her.<P>Don't try to make it sound pratical, Fiero's aren't. Make it sound fun. That, they certainly are!<P>TK||||reg||1
Z||000013||DXR_DAD||09-18-1999||11:56 PM||||jhogans,  Have your wife read the posts from Kel &  DXR_MOM this is a womans point of view on the Fiero. DXR_MOM has fell in love with my car. REMEMBER FUN is what this car is all about, that`s what a sports car is. She has also learned alot from this fourm, and that helps he out alot with my mods. <P>Good luck we're here for ya!!||||reg||1
Z||000014||jhogans||09-28-1999||04:36 PM||||!!!!!!!!! THE WIFE SAID YES !!!!!!!!!!<P>Good things comes to those who are patience.<P>My next door neighbor's boyfriend drives a Honda CRX.  I asked my wife, "what about a car like that". She laughed and said that car is way too small for me also.  I just shrugged it off.  Then lastnight our neighbor came by and  wanted my wife to check out her new furniture.  While she was over there she talked to the boyfried about his CRX and he told her that it was very comfortable and he had plenty of room.  He is 6'3" and ???lbs (big guy).  She came back to the house and said that I can get a Fiero.  She figured that the CRX is about the same size as the Fiero.<P>Boy, was I excited when she told me this.<P>Now, I need some help in finding a good Fiero.  What should I be looking for and looking out for when buying a used Fiero?  I need as much info as I can get.  What should I expect to pay for a used Fiero?<P>Damn, I can't wait until I get one.||||reg||10
Z||000015||87FieroGT||09-28-1999||08:02 PM||||Well I am glad she finally said yes. Congratulations. The kind of things that you need to look for are signs of any previous accidents especially to the rear. There should be no gap between the rear fascia and the tail lights. Make sure that the headlights are in working order, the motor runs smoothly, it is at least a V6, good paint job, lower mileage the better, and hopefully you can find an 88 model. This is my first GT and my third Fiero and I love the cars to death. They are easy to fix up and add modifications to. I hope to one day have an 88 GT because of the upgraded Lotus designed suspension. Anyway good look with your Fiero hunting. I paid about $1700 for mine, but if you want to find an 88 GT with low mileage and in good condition look to spend about $5000. You can find one through an Auto Trader, locally, or hear on the Internet. Once again Happy Fiero hunting.||||reg||10
Z||000016||batboy||09-28-1999||11:11 PM||||Well, since you have already been asking about bigger engine swaps, you probably won't be happy with a 2.5 four cylinder. Fieros with V6's are quite zippy and quick. Sometimes it doesn't sound like it around here at the forum because half of us (or more) are gear-head speed freaks that hate getting spanked by rice-burners. You can't go wrong with a nice 1988 V6 powered Fiero. If you want a bargain, look for a 86-87 SE with a V6. Of course, the GT's are great and hold their value, but again, expect to pay a premuim price for a nice one. Shop around, the deals are out there. Again, test drive a few in order to get an idea what model you'd be happiest with. Fieros are a very personal thing.||||reg||1
Z||000017||BlackGT||09-29-1999||10:18 AM||||JHogans,<BR>That is fantastic ....your wife gave you the ok....My girlfriend wasn`t that impressed when I showed her photos of the car and when<BR>I finally found the one I wanted at a price I was willing to pay I said lets go get it...she said where is it, I said Bassett Va <BR>(we live in Atlanta!) She said why couldn`t you find one closer to home I replied that the folks who have them want you to give them your first born! After kicking and screaming <BR>we went to go get get it....once she listened to the purr of that V6 GT and it looked good she warmed up to the idea. After we got back with it I took her for a ride around Atlanta she grinned the whole time and then stated this is one sexy ride...when do I get a set of keys? Never I replied so she decided that she would make my life a living<BR>hell if I didn`t find her a GT like mine! Well I did and this past monday we picked it up( It was in Columbus Ga and less than half of what I paid for mine!) She drove it around <BR>last night and loved every minute of it. How`s that for a new convert! Most people have a bad misconception of the car but take <BR>them for a drive and watch them get hooked...that`s what happened to me!!  ||||reg||1
Z||000018||jhogans||09-29-1999||10:44 AM||||BlackGT.  I live in Atlanta, GA also.  I'm from Columbus, GA.  How much did you pay for your Fieros?||||reg||1
Z||000019||BlackGT||09-30-1999||11:22 AM||||JHogans,<BR>Well paid $1400 for mine which is right now getting a new engine and clutch along with the ported stock manifolds, and my girlfriend<BR>paid $750 for hers and we haven`t done anything to it yet. You say your in Columbus?<BR>Well this past monday we were in Columbus picking up her car from some dealer on hamilton who is pissed he didn`t ask for more dinero! He called my girl monday afternoon to <BR>ask if my girlfriend would reconsider and choose another car he had `cause he had several people trying to buy the car from under her! In fact there was a guy in the lot<BR>talking to the dealer while he was on the phone with my girl and the guy was willing to double the offer on the car!! Was that you? <BR>Well you know the car is safe at home with us right now but keep looking for "yours". Hey did you know that someone in norcross has pawned an White 88GT! Nutz!!! I don`t care how much of a financial bind I`m in ain`t now way I`m gonna pawn my baby!!! ||||reg||14
Z||000020||jhogans||09-30-1999||11:36 AM||||BGT,<P>That wasn't me that called the dealer  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I live in Atlanta (Lawrenceville) now but I am originally from Columbus, GA.  That guy must be a fooo to pawn his 88 GT.  He must really be hard up for some cash.  Are you a member of the Fiero Club in Atlanta or any other club?<P>You guys were lucky I didn't check in Columbus for a Fiero  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  How did you find out about the car?  Was it through the newspaper?||||reg||1
Z||000021||BlackGT||09-30-1999||11:39 AM||||JHogans,<BR>My eyesite is going or maybe a brain fart...you said you are FROM Columbus and now live in Atlanta right? Well where? I`m in Stone Mountain. There are Fiero nuts all over the ATL so if I were you I would meet up with some fellow owners here in town. The Georgia<BR>Fieros meet once a month at American Pie Restaurant in Sandy Springs on the last sat<BR>each month at about 1:00pm. Go to this site: <A HREF="http://freeyellow.com/members/fiero/index.html" TARGET=_blank>http://freeyellow.com/members/fiero/index.html</A>  <BR>I`m going to join the club when I get around to it but I`m trying to get togeher with one of the club members on sunday to take a look at my girl`s car as well as my exhaust manifolds. E-mail me at: MrToddAG@Excite.com  ||||reg||1
Z||000022||BlackGT||09-30-1999||11:54 AM||||JHogans,<BR>No I did`nt find them thru the newspaper. I found mine on:http://www.hands-on.org/PFKB/<BR>(Pontiac Fiero Knowlegebase classifieds) and I found hers at: <A HREF="http://www.cars.com." TARGET=_blank>www.cars.com.</A>  You can try this site as well and it`s full of info for<BR>hopping up, maintaining, customizing as well as buying a Fiero! Check it out:http://www.angelfire.com/biz/fierosails/info.html||||reg||6
